'' 'typeof( <TYPE> )' WHERE THE TYPE IS SPELLED AS A KEYWORD -- 'typeof( integer )',
'' 'typeof( long ptr )'. The parser kept the operand only when it was a bare IDENT and
'' no expression parser reads a builtin type name, so these were consumed and
'' discarded and the declaration came out untyped. Measured: fbc gives 8, 8, 8, 5, 8
'' for the five below, and every one of them declined.
''
'' quirk/typeof.bas -- the file that exists for this operator -- lost 22 statements to
'' it, and the attempt is speculative in the same way the expression attempt beside it
'' is, so 'typeof( *p )' still reaches the expression parser.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/typeof-typename.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/typeof-typename.out
